<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulster Volunteers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1912">1912</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ulster Volunteers were a Unionist militia founded in 1912 and organised in January 1913 as the Ulster Volunteer Force to resist Home Rule for Ireland. Armed with rifles smuggled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in the Larne gun-running of April 1914, they numbered about 100,000 men, and many later served in the 36th (Ulster) Division in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulster-volunteers.jpg" alt="Ulster Volunteers" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Ulster_Volunteer_Force,_Belfast,_Northern_Ireland,_1914_Q81771.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
